{"name":"Midnight Hour","hex":"#3b484f","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"midnight","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The middle of the night: the sixth temporal hour, equidistant between sunset and sunrise.","Twelve o'clock at night exactly."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Utterly dark or black."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/midnight"},{"term":"hour","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A unit of time of one twenty-fourth of a day (sixty minutes).","A season, moment, or time."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hour"}],"entries":[{"title":"Midnight","blocks":[{"text":"Midnight is the transition time from one day to the next – the moment when the date changes, on the local official clock time for any particular jurisdiction. By clock time, midnight is the opposite of noon, differing from it by 12 hours."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/88/Tour_de_l%27horloge_de_la_gare_de_Metz_%C3%A0_Minuit_%28juin_2019%29_%28cropped%29.JPG/330px-Tour_de_l%27horloge_de_la_gare_de_Metz_%C3%A0_Minuit_%28juin_2019%29_%28cropped%29.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight","wikidata":"Q36402"},{"title":"The Midnight Hour","blocks":[{"text":"The Midnight Hour is a 1985 American made-for-television comedy horror film directed by Jack Bender and starring Shari Belafonte, Lee Montgomery, Kevin McCarthy, LeVar Burton, Peter DeLuise, and Dedee Pfeiffer. Its plot revolves around a small New England town becoming overrun with zombies, witches, vampires, and other demons of hell after a group of teenagers unlocks a centuries-old curse on Halloween."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/8/8a/The_Midnight_Hour_DVD.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Midnight_Hour","wikidata":"Q7751313"},{"title":"Midnight Hour (Skrillex, Boys Noize and Ty Dolla Sign song)","blocks":[{"text":"\"Midnight Hour\" is a song by American record producer Skrillex, German DJ Boys Noize and American singer Ty Dolla Sign. It was released on August 29, 2019, via Owsla and Atlantic. It was nominated for Best Dance Recording at the 2020 Grammy Awards."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/5/5a/Midnight_Hour_Skrillex.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midnight_Hour_(Skrillex%2C_Boys_Noize_and_Ty_Dolla_Sign_song)","wikidata":"Q104901648"},{"title":"Hour","blocks":[{"text":"An hour is a unit of time historically reckoned as 1⁄24 of a day and defined contemporarily as exactly 3,600 seconds. There are 60 minutes in an hour, and 24 hours in a day."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8a/AnalogClockAnimation1_2hands_1h_in_6sec.gif/330px-AnalogClockAnimation1_2hands_1h_in_6sec.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hour","wikidata":"Q25235"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Midnight_Mist.jpg/500px-Midnight_Mist.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4f/Midnight_Mist.jpg/500px-Midnight_Mist.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Photograph of the moon taken at midnight","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMidnight_Mist.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/DigitalClock_1hour.gif/500px-DigitalClock_1hour.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/DigitalClock_1hour.gif/500px-DigitalClock_1hour.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Midnight to 1 a.m. on a 24-hour clock with a digital face","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADigitalClock_1hour.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Bishopstone_sundial.jpg/500px-Bishopstone_sundial.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Bishopstone_sundial.jpg/500px-Bishopstone_sundial.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A 7th-century Saxon tide dial on the porch at Bishopstone in Sussex, with larger crosses marking the canonical hours.[18]","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABishopstone_sundial.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Equatorial_sundial_topview.gif/330px-Equatorial_sundial_topview.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b6/Equatorial_sundial_topview.gif/330px-Equatorial_sundial_topview.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Top view of an equatorial sundial. The hour lines are spaced equally about the circle, and the shadow of the gnomon (a thin cylindrical rod) rotates uniformly. The height of the gnomon is 5⁄12 the outer radius of the dial. This animation depicts the motion of the shadow from 3 a.m. to 9 p.m. on mid-summer's day, when the Sun is at its highest declination (roughly 23.5°). Sunrise and sunset occur at 3 a.m. and 9 p.m. respectively on that day at geographical latitudes near 57.5°, roughly the latitude of Aberdeen or Sitka, Alaska.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AEquatorial_sundial_topview.gif"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/Planispheric_astrolabe.png/500px-Planispheric_astrolabe.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thu